## My life in a nutshell

- Grew up in Tyrol, Austria, with a deep love for snow and an appreciation for the beauty of nature  
- Pursued a career as an engineer, eventually performing qualification tests on spacecraft  
- Eventually realized my heart was still somewhere between snow and alpine ridgelines  
- Shifted back to my roots and earned a Master’s degree in Atmospheric Science in Innsbruck  

Now I find myself in Squamish, Canada, diving into a PhD in Snow Science with the SFU Avalanche Research Program — 
studying snowpack modeling and avalanche forecasting, and chasing the same curiosity that started in the mountains years ago.